---
export const prerender = true;

import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Player manual, Unknown Sender"
  description="How Unknown Sender works — quick reference for players. App, messaging, hints, HELP and SKIP, leaderboard."
  canonicalPath="/player-manual"
>
  <article class="page">
    <div class="wrap-narrow">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>Manual</div>
      <h1>How to play.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Everything you need to know in two minutes. Read this before you set out.
        For safety, kit and weather, see <a href="/before-you-play">Before you play</a>.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2>The basics</h2>
        <p>Unknown Sender is a real-world mystery played on foot. You&rsquo;ll walk
          somewhere between three and five kilometres, follow messages from people
          inside the story, solve puzzles at real locations, and make a final choice
          that decides how it ends. It takes 90&ndash;120 minutes.</p>
        <p>Everything happens through the <strong>Unknown Sender app</strong> on one
          team&rsquo;s phone. You can share the phone as you go, or invite up to three
          teammates so everyone sees the messages on their own device.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Before the day</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Book on this site and pick a team nickname (this shows on the leaderboard).</li>
          <li>Install the <strong>Unknown Sender</strong> app (iOS or Android) and sign
            in with the email you booked with. Your session will be waiting.</li>
          <li>Invite up to three teammates from inside the app if you want them to
            see messages on their own phones.</li>
          <li>Skim <a href="/before-you-play">Before you play</a> for what to wear
            and bring.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Starting the session</h2>
        <p>Head to the start location shown in the app. When you&rsquo;re ready, one
          person taps <strong>Start</strong>. The timer begins and the first message
          arrives.</p>
        <p>You have 90 days from purchase to play, and you don&rsquo;t have to start
          the moment you arrive, take a minute, get a drink, then begin.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How the game plays</h2>
        <p>Messages come from characters inside the story, a Narrator who helps drive
          the plot, and named characters (NPCs) you talk to directly. They&rsquo;ll
          each have a name and a photo, just like a real chat.</p>
        <p>To progress, you&rsquo;ll do one of three things:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Reply with an answer</strong>, a keyword, a number, or a short
            phrase. Case and punctuation don&rsquo;t matter.</li>
          <li><strong>Tap a link</strong> to open a puzzle, an image, or an
            interactive page. Solve what&rsquo;s there, then come back to the chat.</li>
          <li><strong>Make a choice</strong> at branching moments. Different choices
            take you down different paths, some routes are shorter, some are longer.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>When you&rsquo;re stuck</h2>
        <p>Every puzzle has a hint ladder. Wait a bit and hints arrive automatically.
          You can also ask for help or skip:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Send <strong>HELP</strong> to the Narrator to get the current puzzle&rsquo;s
            help message immediately.</li>
          <li>Send <strong>SKIP</strong> to move past a puzzle you&rsquo;re truly stuck
            on. Skips carry a small score penalty but keep the story moving.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Wrong answers don&rsquo;t break anything, try again as many times as you
          need. If a location looks closed or a link won&rsquo;t open, message us on
          <strong>WhatsApp</strong> (details in your booking confirmation).</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>The ending &amp; the leaderboard</h2>
        <p>Near the end you&rsquo;ll be given a final choice, this is the decision
          that defines your ending. There&rsquo;s no single &lsquo;right&rsquo; one.</p>
        <p>When you finish, your team nickname, completion time and score are added to
          the public leaderboard for that game. Phone numbers and personal details are
          never shown.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Rules of thumb</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Cross roads only at proper crossings. Don&rsquo;t use your phone while
            walking near traffic.</li>
          <li>Stay together as a team.</li>
          <li>Nothing in the game will ever ask you to enter private property, climb
            anything, or approach strangers.</li>
          <li>If anywhere feels unsafe or you want to stop, do, the game will still
            be there tomorrow.</li>
          <li>In a genuine emergency, call <strong>999</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <p class="closing">
        See also <a href="/before-you-play">Before you play</a>,
        <a href="/refunds">Refunds</a> and <a href="/terms">Terms</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page { padding: 80px 0; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 3.5rem); margin: 20px 0 20px; letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
  .lede { color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 48px; max-width: 580px; }

  section { margin-bottom: 40px; }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    padding-bottom: 12px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  p { margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink); }
  ul, ol { padding-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  li { margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.55; }
  strong { color: var(--ink); }

  a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  a:hover { color: var(--accent); }

  .closing {
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
</style>
